assistant: Subject: Read unit_amount when price is missing in get_product
In vendor-api-version 2026-10-01, the vendor renamed the product `price` field to `unit_amount`, but the published spec still says `price`. `get_product` only read `p.price ?? null`, so for the new version it quietly returned `price: null`. I added `unit_amount` to the vendor product type and changed the code to use `p.price ?? p.unit_amount ?? null`. I treated `unit_amount` as whole US dollars, not cents, because the one recording I have shows the same value (1199) that v1 returned as `price`. That is the only example, so this rests on a single data point. Old-version responses still go through `price` and return exactly the same output as before. The tool sends the same HTTP requests as before. typecheck, lint and all tests pass, including the repro test. One thing I didn't change: `search_products` also reads only `p.price`, so if the vendor renamed the field in search results too, prices there would come back missing on the new version.

Subject: Read unit_amount when price is missing in get_product
